    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d839">

                <pb facs="0836" n="670" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg670"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 711.5914/130</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Danish Minister to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Danish Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Bar Harbor</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-08-25">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 25, 1916</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to enclose for your
                    inspection the full-power by which His Majesty the King of Denmark was pleased
                    to authorize me to sign the treaty for the cession to the United States of the
                    Danish West India Islands.<anchor n="8" xml:id="d839-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>You will notice that the King’s signature is dated Copenhagen August 1st, 1916
                    and that, in accordance with instructions by cable from the Danish Government, I
                    had the honor of signing the treaty with you at New York on August 4th.</p>
                <p>I beg that after inspection of this document you will be so good as to return it
                    to me, to be kept with the records of this Legation.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">C. Brun</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
